+
+## 2026-07-19 — PS-03D5-5-F1 Account Delete Fail-Closed Correction
+
+### Command Center decision applied
+
+- Option B selected: Account hard deletion must remain fail-closed until an authoritative Assignment History model exists.
+- The current `capacity_customers` table is not authoritative.
+- Its meaning is one-directional:
+  - The presence of a row may prove some historical usage.
+  - The absence of rows cannot prove the absence of Assignment history.
+  - The absence of `capacity_customers` rows must never authorize Account hard deletion.
+- The future authoritative model is expected to involve Order, OrderItem, FulfillmentUnit, Assignment, and Assignment History, but those models are not designed or implemented in this correction.
+- Hard Delete will be reconsidered only in a future Orders / Assignment phase after the canonical Order, OrderItem, FulfillmentUnit, Assignment, Assignment History, migration, permission, and audit contracts are approved.
+- No speculative future phase number is assigned.
+
+### Corrected behavior
+
+- Public production `DELETE /api/accounts/{accountId}` returns HTTP 403 with code `ACCOUNT_OPS_DISABLED` and the exact message: "Account operations are currently disabled".
+- The real delete handler is not invoked by the public route, no validation is performed, and no database writes occur.
+- The internal test-mounted `deleteAccountHandler` validates the Account ID and returns HTTP 404 for missing or already-deleted Accounts.
+- For every existing valid Account, the internal handler returns HTTP 409 with code `ACCOUNT_DELETE_NOT_AVAILABLE` and the exact message: "Account deletion is not available until authoritative assignment history is implemented".
+- The internal delete path performs zero writes whether `capacity_customers` contains no rows, active rows, removed rows, cancelled rows, soft-deleted rows, or any current or historical form.
+- The response contains no secrets, no Customer IDs, no Capacity IDs, and no SQL or internal details.
+
+### Files changed
+
+- `lib/api-spec/openapi.yaml` — removed the successful 204 hard-delete response; the `DELETE /accounts/{accountId}` contract now documents 403 `ACCOUNT_OPS_DISABLED`, 409 `ACCOUNT_DELETE_NOT_AVAILABLE`, 400, 404, and 500.
+- `artifacts/api-server/src/services/account/index.ts` — removed the destructive `deleteAccount` transaction; the service now validates the Account ID and throws `AccountDeleteNotAvailableError`; `capacityCustomersTable` and `inArray` imports removed; `AccountDeleteNotAvailableError` added; `AccountHasAssignmentHistoryError` retained for historical documentation only.
+- `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/accounts.ts` — public DELETE route now returns the exact new 403 message; `deleteAccountHandler` maps `AccountDeleteNotAvailableError` to 409; `AccountHasAssignmentHistoryError` import removed.
+- `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/accounts.disabled.test.ts` — updated public DELETE 403 assertion to expect the new exact message.
+- `artifacts/api-server/src/routes/accounts.delete.test.ts` — rewritten to prove fail-closed behavior: 403 public route, 409 internal handler with zero writes for no history and for active/removed/cancelled/soft-deleted `capacity_customers` rows; removed obsolete hard-delete success, concurrency, identifier-reuse, and destructive trigger tests.
+- `artifacts/api-server/src/lib/account-contract.test.ts` — updated generated-code comment to reflect the removal of the 204 response.
+- `docs/CURRENT_PHASE.md` — status updated to PS-03D5-5-F1 CORRECTION COMPLETE, AWAITING SOURCE REVIEW; parent sub-stage marked as requiring controlled correction and not closed until F1 review.
